---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Skills" description="Find, review, install, update and remove third-party agent skills from inside amber, or headlessly with amber-cli.">
  <NavBar />
  <main>
    <h1>Skills</h1>

    <section class="section">
      <p>
        Amber can find, review, install, update and remove third-party
        <a href="https://skills.sh">skills.sh</a> packages. A skill is a
        <code>SKILL.md</code> package: instructions the model can discover and
        load, not code amber executes. Details (description, license, file tree,
        risk signals) are read from the skill's GitHub repository.
      </p>
      <p>
        Installation is gated on evidence, not vibes: the sheet shows the source,
        file count, size, token cost and body, and a community source needs its
        body read before Enter installs it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider-thick" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Quick start</h2>
      <pre><code>/skills
/skills search tdd
/skills install acme/skills/tdd</code></pre>
      <p>
        The explorer opens on <code>/skills</code>. Type at least two characters
        to search, Enter loads a detail, <code>i</code> opens the install sheet.
        <code>/skills installed</code> opens the shelf of packages already on
        disk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>The install gates</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Review.</strong> With <code>skills_review_required = on</code>
          (the default), a community or unverified source cannot be installed
          until <code>p</code> has shown the body, or <code>x</code> explicitly
          chooses an unread install. Official and audited sources bypass it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Audit.</strong> With <code>skills_audit_required = on</code>, a
          source whose audit is missing or failed needs an explicit override in
          the sheet. The anonymous registry exposes no audits, so the sheet says
          <em>not audited</em> rather than implying a verdict.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Collision.</strong> If the selected scope already holds a
          directory of that name, Enter replaces it, <code>r</code> refuses, and
          Tab switches to the other scope.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Commands</h2>
      <table class="cmd-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>/skills</td><td>Open the Skills Explorer</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills browse</td><td>Open the explorer at an empty search</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills search &lt;query&gt;</td><td>Open the explorer with the query already searched</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills list</td><td>Print the catalog (scope, origin, name, state)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills show &lt;name&gt;</td><td>Print one catalog entry</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills install &lt;id&gt; [--global]</td><td>Fetch a skill and open the install sheet</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills update</td><td>Open the Installed shelf; <code>u</code> checks, <code>u</code> again applies</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills remove &lt;name&gt;</td><td>Open the Installed shelf filtered to that skill</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/skills sources</td><td>Print the registry/GitHub endpoints and cache size</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/set skills review on|off</td><td>Require reading a community body before installing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/set skills audit on|off</td><td>Require an audit verdict before installing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/set skills scope project|global</td><td>Default install scope</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/set skills index skills.sh|none|URL</td><td>Registry source, or none</td></tr>
          <tr><td>/get skills settings</td><td>Show the four acquisition settings</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        In the explorer: <code>j</code>/<code>k</code> move, <code>Enter</code>
        loads a detail, <code>i</code> installs, <code>p</code> previews the body,
        <code>v</code> reports risk signals, <code>u</code> checks/applies an
        update, <code>D</code> removes, <code>x</code>/<code>b</code>
        disable/block, <code>A</code> adopts an unmanaged directory.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Headless</h2>
      <pre><code>amber-cli skills search &lt;query&gt; [--limit N] [--json]
amber-cli skills list [--global] [--json]
amber-cli skills show &lt;name|owner/repo/skill&gt; [--json]
amber-cli skills install &lt;id|owner/repo|url&gt; [--global|--project] [--yes] [--json]
amber-cli skills update [&lt;name&gt;|--all] [--check] [--json]
amber-cli skills remove &lt;name&gt; [--global|--project] [--json]
amber-cli skills sources [--refresh] [--json]</code></pre>
      <p>
        An unattended install refuses a community source without
        <code>--yes</code> and names the review step. <code>--yes</code> is the
        non-interactive form of that consent; the setting never waives it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Settings</h2>
      <pre><code>skills_index = skills.sh          # skills.sh | none | &lt;base-url&gt;
skills_install_scope = project    # project | global
skills_review_required = on
skills_audit_required = off
skills_index_token_env = SKILLS_SH_TOKEN
skills_github_token_env = GITHUB_TOKEN</code></pre>
      <p>
        <code>AMBER_SKILLS_INDEX_URL</code>, <code>AMBER_GITHUB_API_URL</code> and
        <code>AMBER_GITHUB_RAW_URL</code> override the endpoints for one session,
        which is how a self-hosted or air-gapped mirror is used.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Where skills live</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>project scope: <code>&lt;project&gt;/.amber/skills/&lt;name&gt;/</code></li>
        <li>global scope: <code>~/.config/amber/skills/&lt;name&gt;/</code></li>
        <li>provenance: <code>&lt;skills root&gt;/.lock.json</code> (id, source, ref, blob hash, local hash, file/byte counts, enabled state)</li>
        <li>index cache: <code>$XDG_CACHE_HOME/amber/skill-index/</code> (regenerable)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The ledger hashes the installed <code>SKILL.md</code>, so an update
        refuses to overwrite local edits instead of silently discarding them.
        <code>D</code> removes the tree and its ledger entry; overrides such as
        <code>block</code> deliberately survive.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        A <code>SKILL.md</code> is untrusted instruction text that the model will
        follow. Amber sanitizes every remote string before it reaches the
        terminal or the ledger, reports shell/network/path signals in the body,
        and keeps the review gate on by default so the text is visible before it
        is trusted. Installing a skill does not execute it: the body loads only
        when the model asks for it, and a blocked skill is never listed.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
